# Lutri, the Spellchaser copies Bot1's Collective Brutality, escalated once (Bot1 discards an Island) to choose
# "Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn" at Bot2's Llanowar Elves and "Target opponent loses 2 life and you gain 2
# life" at Bot2. The copy has the same two modes and pays nothing, the escalate cost included (CR 707.10, 707.10c,
# 702.120a: no modes question, no discard). Bot1 may choose new targets for it: the creature becomes Bot2's Ornithopter;
# Bot2 is the only opponent, so the drain's target cannot change and is not asked (the next answer is priority). The copy
# resolves first: Ornithopter dies and Bot2 loses 2; then the original: the Elves die and Bot2 loses 2 more. Bot1 gains 4.
# Left on its old targets, the copy would give the Elves -4/-4 and Ornithopter would survive.

